# Skip link

Let keyboard users bypass repeated navigation and reach the main content.

These are civica reference implementations for component authors. They do not replace native Home Assistant behaviour or demonstrate a connection to a live home.

## When to use it

Use a skip link at the start of a standalone page with repeated header or navigation controls. Its destination is the main content, not the first decorative heading.

## When not to use it

Do not add duplicate skip links inside every card or point to an absent fragment. A link that scrolls without moving focus may leave the keyboard user at the start of navigation.

## Home Assistant adaptation

The civica documentation shell supplies page-level navigation. In Home Assistant, routing and shadow roots require integration with the native focus target; a fragment in one shadow tree cannot automatically focus another. Do not claim a global skip enhancement from an isolated HTML example.

## Accessibility and behaviour

Keep the link visually hidden until focused, then reveal it with strong contrast. Use a real anchor and a focusable main target, commonly tabindex="-1". Its position should let it skip the back link and other repeated controls as well.

