## Check the implementation

Open the standalone example, press Tab and activate the skip link. Verify the next keyboard action begins in main content. Repeat after route changes, with zoom and with a screen reader.

Use the [civica accessibility checks](../accessibility/testing.html) and compare the rendered result in light and dark modes, Vivid and Muted tones, and at 320 CSS pixels. The example markup is a starting point; a theme alone does not add its application logic.

## Source and related guidance

[NHS skip link](https://service-manual.nhs.uk/design-system/components/skip-link) informs the component choice and interaction guidance. The examples use shared GOV.UK primitives or original civica markup, Arial typography and civica assets. NHS logos and service identity are not used.

